Commodore 64 ROMs
=================

Downloaded from http://www.unusedino.de/ec64/technical2.html
Credited in turn to ftp://ftp.funet.fi/pub/cbm

basic.rom
---------
Commodore 64 BASIC V2. The first and only revision.

kernal.rom
----------
Commodore 64 KERNAL ROM Revision 3. The last revision, also used in
the C128's C64 mode.

character.rom
-------------
The character generator ROM.

kernal-sx64.rom
---------------
The SX-64's KERNAL, 251104-04. It boots with the SX-64's banner and
colours, and loads from device 8 rather than tape. C64.new(kernal:
:sx64) fits it, as --model sx64 does.

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/c64/kernal.sx.251104-04.bin
SHA-1 aa136e91ecf3c5ac64f696b3dbcbfc5ba0871c98.

kernal-pet64.rom
----------------
The KERNAL of the PET 64, 4064 and Educator 64, 901246-01. It boots
with the "**** COMMODORE 4064  BASIC V2.0 ****" banner and a white
cursor, and its interrupt routine keeps the border, background and
sprite colours black unless bit 7 of $0286 is set. C64.new(kernal:
:pet64) fits it, as --model pet64 does.

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/c64/kernal.4064.901246-01.bin
MD5 da92801e3a03b005b746a4dd0b639c7c.

c64gs.rom
---------
The C64GS's BASIC and KERNAL, 390852-01, 16 KB: BASIC for $A000-$BFFF
followed by the KERNAL for $E000-$FFFF. Its BASIC is 901226-01's but
for 30 unused bytes. Its KERNAL is 901227-03's with most changes in
$F72C-$FC92, the cassette routines' place, and many jumps redirected to
I/O error 5. C64.new(kernal: :gs) fits both, as --model c64gs does.

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/c64/64gs.390852-01.bin
MD5 049e657afafbdd802e8c6a4f88f3d730.

dos1541.rom
-----------
The 1541 disk drive's DOS 2.6, 16 KB for $C000-$FFFF: 325302-01
($C000-$DFFF) followed by 901229-05 ($E000-$FFFF). Drives::Model1541 loads it.

Both halves downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/drives/new/1541/
(1541-c000.325302-01.bin and 1541-e000.901229-05.bin) and concatenated.
SHA-1 ab16f56989b27d89babe5f89c5a8cb3da71a82f0.

dos1571.rom
-----------
The 1571 disk drive's DOS 3.0, 310654-05, 32 KB for $8000-$FFFF.
Drives::Model1571 loads it.

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/drives/new/1571/1571-rom.310654-05.bin
SHA-1 f1be619c106641a685f6609e4d43d6fc9eac1e70.

dos1581.rom
-----------
The 1581 disk drive's DOS, 318045-02, 32 KB for $8000-$FFFF.
Drives::Model1581 loads it.

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/drives/new/1581/1581-rom.318045-02.bin
SHA-1 01228eae6f066bd9b7b2b6a7fa3f667e41dad393.

dos1551.rom
-----------
The 1551 disk drive's DOS 2.6, 318008-01, 16 KB for $C000-$FFFF.
Drives::Model1551 loads it.

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/drives/new/1551/1551.318008-01.bin
SHA-1 fae3c788ad9a6cc2dbdfbcf6c0264b2ca921d55e.

Commodore VIC-20 ROMs
=====================

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/vic20/
Vic20::Bus maps them.

vic20/basic.rom
---------------
VIC-20 BASIC V2, 901486-01, for $C000-$DFFF.
SHA-1 587d1e90950675ab6b12d91248a3f0d640d02e8d.

vic20/kernal-pal.rom
--------------------
The PAL KERNAL, 901486-07, for $E000-$FFFF.
SHA-1 ce0137ed69f003a299f43538fa9eee27898e621e.

vic20/kernal-ntsc.rom
---------------------
The NTSC KERNAL, 901486-06, for $E000-$FFFF.
SHA-1 06de7ec017a5e78bd6746d89c2ecebb646efeb19.

vic20/character.rom
-------------------
The character generator ROM, 901460-03, for $8000-$8FFF.
SHA-1 4fd85ab6647ee2ac7ba40f729323f2472d35b9b4.

Commodore 128 ROMs
==================

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/c128/
C128::Bus maps them in C128 mode. C64 mode runs basic.rom, kernal.rom
and character.rom above.

c128/basic.rom
--------------
BASIC 7.0, 318022-02 (basic.318022-02.bin), 32 KB: the low half for
$4000-$7FFF followed by the high half for $8000-$BFFF.
SHA-1 953dcdf5784a6b39ef84dd6fd968c7a03d8d6816.

c128/kernal.rom
---------------
318020-05 (kernal.318020-05.bin), 16 KB: the screen editor for
$C000-$CFFF, the Z80 BIOS for $D000-$DFFF and the KERNAL for
$E000-$FFFF.
SHA-1 ceb6e1a1bf7e08eb9cbc651afa29e26adccf38ab.

c128/character.rom
------------------
The character generator ROM, 390059-01 (characters.390059-01.bin),
8 KB: the C64's set, the same as character.rom, followed by the C128's.
SHA-1 29ed066d513f2d5c09ff26d9166ba23c2afb2b3f.

Commodore 264 series ROMs
=========================

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/plus4/
for the Plus/4, the C16 and the C116, which share BASIC and the KERNAL.
Nothing maps them yet.

plus4/basic.rom
---------------
BASIC 3.5, 318006-01 (basic.318006-01.bin), for $8000-$BFFF in ROM
bank 0.
SHA-1 161c96b4ad20f3a4f2321808e37a5ded26a135dd.

plus4/kernal-pal.rom
--------------------
The PAL KERNAL, 318004-05 (kernal.318004-05.bin), for $C000-$FFFF in
ROM bank 0, with the character set from $D000.
SHA-1 7c7e07f016391174a557e790c4ef1cbe33512cdb.

plus4/kernal-ntsc.rom
---------------------
The NTSC KERNAL, 318005-05 (kernal.318005-05.bin), for $C000-$FFFF in
ROM bank 0.
SHA-1 a3d9e5be091b98de39a046ab167fb7632d053682.

plus4/function-low.rom
----------------------
The Plus/4's 3-plus-1 function ROM, low half, 317053-01
(3-plus-1.317053-01.bin), for $8000-$BFFF in ROM bank 1.
SHA-1 3b69f6e7cb4c18bb08e203fb18b7dabfa853390f.

plus4/function-high.rom
-----------------------
The Plus/4's 3-plus-1 function ROM, high half, 317054-01
(3-plus-1.317054-01.bin), for $C000-$FFFF in ROM bank 1.
SHA-1 0ad7ac2db7da692d972e586ca0dfd747d82c7693.

Commodore PET/CBM ROMs
======================

Downloaded from
https://www.zimmers.net/anonftp/pub/cbm/firmware/computers/pet/
Each BASIC and KERNAL pair is one ROM set, and the editors and the
character sets are files of their own, so a model's stock set and the
upgrade ROMs Commodore sold can be picked apart. Nothing maps them yet.

pet/basic1.rom
--------------
BASIC 1 for $C000-$DFFF, four 2K chips concatenated:
901447-09 (rom-2-c000.901447-09.bin, the revision that replaced
901447-01), 901447-02, 901447-03 and 901447-04 (rom-1-c800, rom-1-d000,
rom-1-d800).
SHA-1 3be9cd41b646fefa00d80f1c3433a06146e97c59.

pet/editor1.rom
---------------
The BASIC 1 screen editor, 901447-05 (rom-1-e000.901447-05.bin), for
$E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 f02f5fb492ba93dbbd390f24c10f7a832dec432a.

pet/kernal1.rom
---------------
The BASIC 1 KERNAL for $F000-$FFFF, 901447-06 and 901447-07
(rom-1-f000.901447-06.bin, rom-1-f800.901447-07.bin) concatenated.
SHA-1 32dc08828e88c74d6433156e64d402b564556308.

pet/characters1.rom
-------------------
The 2001's character generator, 901447-08 (characters-1.901447-08.bin),
with upper and lower case swapped against 901447-10.
SHA-1 3e067cc621e4beafca2b90cb8f6dba975df2855b.

pet/basic2.rom
--------------
BASIC 2 for $C000-$DFFF, 901465-01 and 901465-02
(basic-2-c000.901465-01.bin, basic-2-d000.901465-02.bin) concatenated.
The 2K chips of the 6540 boards (rom-3-*) hold the same bytes.
SHA-1 9322a9f0354b9049847d98d3a045fbec860a6264.

pet/kernal2.rom
---------------
The BASIC 2 KERNAL, 901465-03 (kernal-2.901465-03.bin), for $F000-$FFFF.
SHA-1 38742bdf449f629bcba6276ef24d3daeb7da6e84.

pet/editor2-n.rom
-----------------
The BASIC 2 editor for the graphics keyboard, 901447-24
(edit-2-n.901447-24.bin), for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 5e5502ce32f5a7e387d65efe058916282041e54b.

pet/editor2-b.rom
-----------------
The BASIC 2 editor for the business keyboard, 901474-01
(edit-2-b.901474-01.bin), for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 174ace3a8c0348cd21d39cc864e2adc58b0101a9.

pet/characters2.rom
-------------------
The character generator of BASIC 2 and 4 machines, 901447-10
(characters-2.901447-10.bin).
SHA-1 0157a2d55b7ac4eaeb38475889ebeea52e2593db.

pet/basic4.rom
--------------
BASIC 4 for $B000-$DFFF, 901465-23, 901465-20 and 901465-21
(basic-4-b000.901465-23.bin, basic-4-c000.901465-20.bin,
basic-4-d000.901465-21.bin) concatenated. 901465-23 is the patched
$B000 chip that replaced 901465-19. The 8296's 324746-01 holds the same
four chips.
SHA-1 d70bec479e1e3a0d0908a4897066e9959bbc11c8.

pet/kernal4.rom
---------------
The BASIC 4 KERNAL, 901465-22 (kernal-4.901465-22.bin), for
$F000-$FFFF.
SHA-1 96a0fa56e0c937da92971d9c99d504e44e898806.

pet/editor4-n.rom
-----------------
The BASIC 4 editor for the graphics keyboard without a CRTC, 901447-29
(edit-4-n.901447-29.bin), for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 e88f56e5c54b0e8d8d4e8cb39a4647c803c1f51c.

pet/editor4-b.rom
-----------------
The BASIC 4 editor for the business keyboard without a CRTC, 901474-02
(edit-4-b.901474-02.bin), for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 0ca5c4e8f532f914cb0bf86ea9900f20f0a655ce.

pet/editor4-40-n-50hz.rom
-------------------------
The 4032's 50 Hz editor, 40 columns on a CRTC, graphics keyboard,
901498-01 (edit-4-40-n-50Hz.901498-01.bin), for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 05af284c914d53a52987b5f602466de75765f650.

pet/editor4-40-n-60hz.rom
-------------------------
The 4032's 60 Hz editor, 901499-01 (edit-4-40-n-60Hz.901499-01.bin),
for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 8cbf086c1ce4dfb2a2fe24c47476dfb878493dee.

pet/editor4-80-b-50hz.rom
-------------------------
The 8032's 50 Hz editor, 80 columns on a CRTC, business keyboard,
901474-04, the chip dated 3681
(edit-4-80-b-50Hz.901474-04-3681.bin), for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 7040b283ba39e9630e3d147f7d076b7abc39bc70.

zimmers.net has three dumps of 901474-04 that differ. This one is the
60 Hz 901474-03 below with the 50 Hz jiffy clock patch at $E431-$E441
and $E455, the CRTC's vertical registers (R4, R5 and R7) changed in both
of its register tables at $E72A, and the byte at $E787 changed to keep
the ROM's byte sum at $8A, the same as 901474-03's. The line length (R0)
stays the 60 Hz editor's. A second chip, dated 0384, reads the same
(8296/edit-50hz-324243-02b.txt). The -0283 dump changes R0 and sums to
$AE, and the _alt dump changes R0 and $E787.

pet/editor4-80-b-50hz-0283.rom
------------------------------
The 8032's other 50 Hz editor, 901474-04, the chip dated 0283
(edit-4-80-b-50Hz.901474-04-0283.bin), for $E000-$E7FF, which
--editor 4-80-b-50hz-0283 fits. It differs from the 3681 dump only in
the CRTC's register tables at $E72A and $E73C: lines of 64 cycles (R0
63) and frames of 313 lines, with nine scanlines a character row.
SHA-1 81975eab31a8f4f51ae2a20d099a567c7b3f2dd1.

pet/editor4-80-b-60hz.rom
-------------------------
The 8032's 60 Hz editor, 901474-03 (edit-4-80-b-60Hz.901474-03.bin),
for $E000-$E7FF.
SHA-1 c605fa343fd77c73cbe1e0e9567e2f014f6e7e30.
